From: X710 bring-up <bringup@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: qcom-geni: log the bus line levels when a transfer fails

geni_i2c_err_misc() already reads SE_GENI_IOS - the SDA and SCL line levels -
but only prints it with dev_dbg, which is compiled out here, so a failed
transfer reports nothing but -ENXIO.

That ambiguity has cost several hardware tests.  The driver this board's stock
kernel uses on this bus (i2c-msm-geni.c, CONFIG_I2C_MSM_GENI) reads the same
register before every transfer and returns -ENXIO when SCL and SDA are not both
high - "IO lines in bad state, Power the slave" - so -ENXIO can mean either a
real address NACK or a bus that something is holding down, and this port has
never been able to tell them apart: its own line-level diagnostics cannot claim
gpio72/106 while the controller owns them and print -1 instead.

Print the line levels, the master command and the GENI status at info level on
the error path.  The check, the error codes and the recovery path are untouched.
---
diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c
index d2f5055b0..5953b2a7a 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c
@@ -234,10 +234,21 @@ static void geni_i2c_err_misc(struct geni_i2c_dev *gi2c)
 		rx_st = readl_relaxed(gi2c->se.base + SE_GENI_RX_FIFO_STATUS);
 		tx_st = readl_relaxed(gi2c->se.base + SE_GENI_TX_FIFO_STATUS);
 	}
-	dev_dbg(gi2c->se.dev, "DMA:%d tx_stat:0x%x, rx_stat:0x%x, irq-stat:0x%x\n",
-		dma, tx_st, rx_st, m_stat);
-	dev_dbg(gi2c->se.dev, "m_cmd:0x%x, geni_status:0x%x, geni_ios:0x%x\n",
-		m_cmd, geni_s, geni_ios);
+	/*
+	 * Bits 0 and 1 of SE_GENI_IOS are the SDA and SCL line levels: 0x3 means
+	 * both are high, i.e. an idle bus, so a failure is a real address NACK;
+	 * anything else means something is holding a line down.  This is the
+	 * distinction the downstream driver this board's stock kernel uses makes
+	 * before every transfer, and it is invisible at dev_dbg here.
+	 */
+	dev_info(gi2c->se.dev, "DMA:%d tx_stat:0x%x, rx_stat:0x%x, irq-stat:0x%x\n",
+		 dma, tx_st, rx_st, m_stat);
+	dev_info(gi2c->se.dev,
+		 "m_cmd:0x%x, geni_status:0x%x, geni_ios:0x%x (%s)\n",
+		 m_cmd, geni_s, geni_ios,
+		 (geni_ios & 0x3) == 0x3 ? "scl/sda high, idle bus" :
+					   "scl/sda NOT both high");
+
 }
 
 static void geni_i2c_err(struct geni_i2c_dev *gi2c, int err)
